Built a custom Linux SLAB allocator module today.

Implemented:
- kmem_cache
- shrinker API
- lock-protected object tracking
- cache-aligned kernel objects
- reclaim under memory pressure

Why this matters:

Most people use malloc().
Kernel engineers optimize allocation latency,
cache locality,
fragmentation,
and reclaim behavior.

That’s where SLAB comes in.

ASCII view:

        Userspace malloc()
                 |
          +------v------+
          | kmalloc()   |
          +------v------+
                 |
         +-------v--------+
         | SLAB Allocator |
         +-------v--------+
                 |
      +----------+----------+
      | object reuse pools  |
