What Problem This Program Solves

This module demonstrates how the Linux kernel efficiently manages frequently allocated small objects.

Without slab allocators:

repeated kmalloc/kfree
fragmentation increases
CPU cache misses increase
allocation latency increases
reclaim logic becomes harder

This module solves:

1. Fast Object Allocation

Objects are pre-structured and cache-aligned.

2. Reduced Fragmentation

SLAB reuses object pools efficiently.

3. Better CPU Cache Locality

SLAB_HWCACHE_ALIGN improves access speed.

4. Memory Pressure Handling

Shrinker allows reclaim under low-memory conditions.

5. Scalable Kernel Object Management

Used in real kernel subsystems like:

dentry cache
inode cache
networking buffers
task structures
